@title Presentation Sections

@s Empty explicit section
@s


@s Prose only
This section contains prose and no code.

@s Code only
--- Code only
code_only();
---

@s Prose and code
The prose and code share one presentation section.
--- Prose and code
prose_and_code();
---

@s Prose after code
The first prose block.
--- Prose then code
first();
---
The second prose block starts an implicit section.

@s Prose and consecutive code
The prose accompanies the first code block.
--- Prose code one
one();
---
--- Prose code two
two();
---

@s Code prose code
--- Code prose first
first();
---
The prose after code starts another presentation section.
--- Code prose second
second();
---

@s Three code blocks
--- Three one
one();
---
--- Three two
two();
---
--- Three three
three();
---

@s Hidden blocks and commands
Visible prose precedes hidden and visible code.
@code_type rust .rs
--- Hidden base --- noWeave
hidden_base();
---
--- Visible after hidden
visible();
---
@comment_type // %s
--- Hidden base --- noWeave +=
hidden_addition();
---

@s Hidden code between prose blocks
First visible prose.
--- Hidden separator --- noWeave
hidden_separator();
---
Second visible prose still starts an implicit section.

@s Hidden-only explicit section
--- Hidden only --- noWeave
not_rendered();
---

@s Relationships
The forward prose reference @{Target} links to the first visible definition.
--- Target
base();
---
--- Target +=
addition();
---
--- Target :=
replacement();
---
--- Use target
@{Target}
---
